-- title:
--   Conjugate Gauss rings are unramified over Γ₀(M'): case q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=2$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ not divisible by $q$, and a field $L$ of characteristic zero containing an element $\zeta$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield `xHFunctionField` of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ at level $q^2M'$ with subgroup `levelH` $q$ $M'$, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$; that field is itself generated by the quotients of integral $q$-expansions of two modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with nonzero denominator. Let $K_0 \le K$ be the analogous base change of the field generated by such quotients for $\Gamma_0(M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ that can be written as $x/y$ with $x, y \in A[[T]]$ and $y$ of nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $O_0$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ described by the same condition. Let $\tau$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$, and assume that an element of $K_0$ lies in $O_0$ precisely when its image in $K$ lies in $\tau^{-1}(W_0)$, so that $O_0 \to \tau^{-1}(W_0)$ is well defined. Then the ramification index of the maximal ideal of $\tau^{-1}(W_0)$ over the maximal ideal of $O_0$ equals $1$.
--
--   This records that, at $q=2$, every $L$-automorphism conjugate of the Gauss (Igusa) valuation ring attached to the cusp $\infty$ on the level-$q^2M'$ curve is unramified over the corresponding Gauss ring of $X_0(M')$. It feeds the existence statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_comap_eq_and_ramificationIdx_eq_one_and_isSeparable_of_over_gauss_gamma0_mul_xH_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_comap_eq_and_ramificationIdx_eq_one_and_isSeparable_of_over_gauss_gamma0_mul_xH_of_eq_two), part of the local analysis of the covering of $X_0(M')$ by the level-$q^2M'$ curve above the cusp $\infty$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_ramificationIdx_comap_gauss_eq_one_of_levelH_of_eq_two.lean

